Recommended bottom navigation: Home, History, prominent Scan action, Saved, Profile. If five destinations crowd small screens, use four destinations and a central scan action or move Saved into Home/History.
7. Screen specifications
- Splash: Floral White, botanical mark, ScanSafe wordmark, “Scan. Check. Stay Safe.”
- Onboarding: “Know what’s inside”; “Understand the evidence”; “Make informed choices”; Skip and Get started.
- Home: wordmark, optional search, prominent Scan a product card, manual entry, recent scans, saved products, bottom navigation.
- Scanner: camera preview, capture, flash, close, gallery import, alignment frame, permission rationale, retake/crop/multiple images.
- Text review: original image, editable OCR text, uncertainty highlights, Retake and Analyze actions; preserve raw OCR separately.
- Progress: steps for reading label, identifying ingredients, checking evidence, preparing report; no fabricated percentage.
- Result: overview, findings, preferences, unmatched items, sources, Save/Share/Report issue. Prefer “No relevant concern identified in checked sources” over a universal “Safe” claim.
- Finding detail: category, explanation, evidence strength, conditions, jurisdiction, source and date.
- Unknown ingredient: show exact text; edit/retry/manual lookup; state that no match proves neither harm nor safety.
- Product/ingredient details: Overview, Ingredients, Findings, Evidence sources; never invent unavailable product details.
- History: search/filter, date, label/product, report status, delete.
- Saved products: list/watchlist and last scan date; claim monitoring only if implemented.
- Profile: preferences, region, subscription, notifications, privacy, export, account deletion, support and legal.
- Paywall: exact benefits, price, billing period, renewal/trial terms, restore purchases and clear close behavior.
8. Reusable components
PrimaryButton, SecondaryButton, IconButton, SearchField, IngredientInput, IngredientChip, FindingCard, EvidenceSourceRow, ProductSummaryCard, ScanHistoryItem, StatusLabel, ConfidenceIndicator, EmptyState, ErrorState, PermissionRationale, LoadingStepList, BottomNavigation, ConfirmationDialog, SubscriptionPlanCard.

Define pressed, focused, disabled, loading, and error states where relevant.
9. Error states
Design for denied camera permission, offline, unreadable image, empty/partial OCR, unmatched ingredient, unavailable evidence source, analysis outage, quota reached, expired session, interrupted upload, failed report, billing pending/failed, empty history and empty saved list. A technical failure must never become a safety finding.
10. Accessibility
Support TalkBack, logical focus order, font scaling, 48 dp target guidance, contrast checks, non-color status cues, small and large screens, landscape and reduced motion.
11. Tone
Use calm language such as “The evidence is limited” and “We couldn’t identify this ingredient.” Avoid unsupported alarmist claims or “100% safe.”   ScanSafe.AI — Technical Architecture
