4. API behavior
- Validate every request.
- Use stable error codes such as IMAGE_UNREADABLE, INGREDIENTS_REQUIRED, EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE, QUOTA_EXCEEDED.
- Include correlation IDs.
- Paginate lists and cap page sizes.
- Use idempotency for scan creation, analysis and billing-sensitive mutations.
- Apply rate limits and verify ownership on every resource.
- An upstream timeout must not become a safety finding.
5. Scan states
Normal: created → image_received → extracting → awaiting_confirmation → analyzing → completed.

Failure/terminal: image_rejected, extraction_failed, analysis_failed, cancelled, deleted. Enforce valid transitions server-side.
6. Evidence processing
Evidence records require review/approval. Store source organization, URL, jurisdiction, effective/review dates and evidence summary. Use deterministic rules for restrictions/preferences. Validate AI claims against retrieved source IDs. Persist a versioned report snapshot.
7. Billing and quotas
Verify purchases with the provider; reconcile notifications; enforce quota server-side; handle pending, active, grace, cancelled, expired, refunded and revoked states as relevant; support restore purchases. Do not trust client entitlement values.
8. Security/privacy
TLS, managed secrets, private object storage, expiring links, least privilege, strict authorization, file validation, rate limiting, redacted logs, retention/deletion jobs, backup recovery tests and admin audit logs.
9. Testing
Unit tests for parser/matcher/rules/state machine; integration tests for DB/storage/auth/billing; API contract tests; IDOR/authorization tests; upload abuse tests; idempotency/retry tests; deletion/export tests; representative load tests; AI grounding and unsupported-claim tests.
10. Operations
Dashboard API latency/errors, OCR failures, matching coverage, unknown rate, analysis duration/cost, source failures, queue backlog, entitlement mismatches, deletion failures and feedback volume. canSafe.AI — Android App Flow
