3. Scan states
idle, permission_explanation, camera_ready, capturing, image_quality_check, extracting, awaiting_text_review, analyzing, completed, failed_retryable, failed_terminal, cancelled.

Keep state in a ViewModel; restore safe progress through configuration changes. Do not save large bitmaps in instance state—persist a URI/reference as appropriate.
4. Result actions
Open findings and sources; correct text and re-run; save/remove scan; share a limited report; report an issue; start another scan. Sharing must not expose private preferences by default.
5. Permissions
Request camera permission only after the user chooses Scan. Explain the purpose. If denied, offer gallery/manual entry. For permanent denial, provide a Settings route rather than repeatedly prompting. Request notifications when a user enables a feature that needs them.
6. Account flow
Possible policy: guest scans with a limited quota; sign-in for cross-device history, cloud saves or subscription sync. Explain stored data and deletion. Clear sensitive local cache on sign-out as appropriate.
7. Premium flow
User reaches quota or opens Premium → show features/price/renewal → launch billing UI → verify purchase on backend → refresh entitlement. Handle pending/failed states without granting unverified access; support restore purchases.
