Database: PostgreSQL | Status: Proposed logical schema
1. Principles
- Stable IDs and foreign keys.
- Preserve raw OCR separately from corrected text.
- Record evidence provenance and review status.
- Version reports, rules and evidence.
- Separate preferences from evidence findings.
- Minimize image and sensitive data retention.
2. Entity relationships
```mermaid
erDiagram
 USERS ||--o{ USER_PREFERENCES : has
 USERS ||--o{ SCANS : creates
 SCANS ||--o{ SCAN_IMAGES : contains
 SCANS ||--o{ EXTRACTED_INGREDIENTS : extracts
 SCANS ||--o{ ANALYSIS_REPORTS : produces
 INGREDIENTS ||--o{ INGREDIENT_ALIASES : has
 INGREDIENTS ||--o{ INGREDIENT_EVIDENCE : supported_by
 EVIDENCE_SOURCES ||--o{ INGREDIENT_EVIDENCE : contains
 ANALYSIS_REPORTS ||--o{ REPORT_FINDINGS : includes
 INGREDIENTS ||--o{ REPORT_FINDINGS : refers_to
 USERS ||--o{ SUBSCRIPTIONS : owns
 USERS ||--o{ FEEDBACK_REPORTS : submits
 USERS ||--o{ AUDIT_EVENTS : generates
```
3. Tables
users
id UUID PK, auth_provider_subject UNIQUE, optional email, account_status, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at. Avoid storing passwords if managed auth is used.
user_preferences
id, user_id FK, preference_type, preference_value JSONB or normalized relation, is_enabled, timestamps. Restrict access to sensitive preferences.
scans
id, nullable user_id, category, status, region_code, raw_ocr_text, corrected_ingredients_text, ocr_engine_version, timestamps, deleted_at, retention_expires_at.
scan_images
id, scan_id FK, private storage_key, MIME type, size, dimensions, timestamps, deletion/retention fields. Never use permanent public image URLs.
ingredients
id, canonical_name, category, description, record_status, timestamps.
ingredient_aliases
id, ingredient_id FK, alias_text, normalized_alias, language_code, source. Index normalized aliases and enforce appropriate uniqueness.
extracted_ingredients
id, scan_id FK, raw_text, normalized_text, nullable ingredient_id FK, match_status, match_confidence, user_confirmed, position_index, created_at. Match confidence is not a health-risk score.
evidence_sources
id, organization, title, URL, source type, jurisdiction, published/retrieved dates, license notes, review status.
ingredient_evidence
id, ingredient_id FK, evidence_source_id FK, finding type, evidence summary/strength, conditions, jurisdiction, effective dates, reviewed date, reviewer, version, approval status.
jurisdiction_rules
id, ingredient_id FK, jurisdiction code, rule type, rule_payload JSONB, effective dates, source evidence FK, rule version, approval status.
analysis_reports
id, scan_id FK, report status, summary status, evidence dataset version, rules version, optional prompt/model versions, created time, limitations JSONB.
report_findings
id, report_id FK, nullable ingredient_id FK, extracted_ingredient_id FK, finding type, status, explanation, jurisdiction, created time. Prefer a report_finding_evidence join table for referential integrity.
subscriptions
id, user_id FK, provider, provider purchase ID, product ID, status, current period end, verified time, timestamps. Verify entitlements server-side.
usage_quotas
id, user/guest identifier as appropriate, period start/end, scan count, quota limit, plan code. Use atomic/transactional updates.
feedback_reports
id, nullable user/scan/report IDs, category, description, status, created/reviewed times.
audit_events
id, nullable actor, action, entity type/ID, correlation ID, redacted JSONB metadata, created time. Do not log secrets or unnecessary personal data.
4. Indexes to consider
- scans(user_id, created_at DESC)
- scan_images(scan_id)
- extracted_ingredients(scan_id, position_index)
- ingredient_aliases(normalized_alias)
- ingredient_evidence(ingredient_id, approval_status, jurisdiction)
- analysis_reports(scan_id, created_at DESC)
- subscriptions(user_id, status)
- feedback_reports(status, created_at)
Choose final indexes from measured query patterns.
5. Retention and deletion
Define separate retention for images, OCR text, corrected lists, reports, analytics, audit events and backups. Account deletion should enqueue deletion of user-linked data with retries and auditable completion. Document backup expiry and legal exceptions; do not promise immediate backup deletion unless implemented.
6. Integrity and migrations
Use version-controlled migrations, foreign keys, unique constraints, transactions for report persistence/quota consumption, immutable evidence publication versions and tested backup restoration. Never overwrite the evidence/rule versions used by prior reports.
